{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1097685-can-you-reverse-engineer-a-one-shot","id":1097685,"title":"Can you Reverse Engineer a One-Shot?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-27T21:37:09-07:00","id":1097685,"title":"Can you Reverse Engineer a One-Shot?","content":"This is something I asked in another thread, but can you reverse engineer a One-Shot? Flowers Of Hell brings the issue up, and goes both ways about it - there are specifically penalties for reverse engineering them on page 144, specifically &quot;If the gadget is a one-shot or a knock-off, each roll suffers a \u20132 penalty.&quot; and even states &quot;One-shots with Exploited effects do not cause as disastrous effects, but do release aetheric energies that might draw the attention of agents of the God-Machine at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion.&quot;.<br /> <br /> However, on page 149 it says &quot;Due to their fragile and temporary nature, a demon can\u2019t reverse-engineer a one-shot gadget to learn the Embed or Exploit behind its creation, or to create a lambda.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't know whether this is an errata issue, or whether there are more reasons to reverse engineer a gadget that just to learn its Embeds/Exploits or make a Lambda. Does anyone know, or have anything to weigh in with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T15:42:50-07:00","id":1097890,"title":"","content":"Either case sadly is as valid as the other by RAW however since one-shots can be made for less xp (1xp for a # equal to primum potentially) I would say it shouldn't. However, since 144 gives the penalty and makes it more likely to fail I cannot say that it is too much to allow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}